{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli a noble family that ruled the County of Tripoli. He was the son of Pons of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was born around 1150 AD and died in 1187 AD.\n\n* **Family Background** *\nRaymond III's father Pons of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 AD until his death in 1184 AD. Pons was a member of the House of Toulouse and was a vassal of the King of Jerusalem. Raymond III's mother Hodierna of Jerusalem was a member of the royal family of Jerusalem. She was a daughter of Melisende of Jerusalem and Fulk of Anjou.\n\nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli after the death of his father Pons of Tripoli in 1184 AD. He was still a minor at the time and was under the regency of his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III married Isabella of Jerusalem in 1173 AD. Isabella was a member of the royal family of Jerusalem and a daughter of Amalric I of Jerusalem and Agnes of Courtenay.\n\n* **Military Campaigns** *\nRaymond III was involved in several military campaigns during his reign as Count of Tripoli. He participated in the Third Crusade and fought against the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. Raymond III was also involved in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 AD where the Crusader forces were defeated by the Ayyubid forces. After the defeat at Hattin Raymond III was forced to surrender the County of Tripoli to Saladin. He was imprisoned and later released.\n\n* **Legacy** *\nRaymond III's reign as Count of Tripoli was marked by several military campaigns and the eventual loss of the county to the Ayyubid forces. He died in 1187 AD and was succeeded by his son Bohemond VI of Antioch and Tripoli. Raymond III's legacy is marked by his involvement in the Third Crusade and the Battle of Hattin. He is also remembered as the last ruler of the House of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token":